<title>SINGAPORE: United Overseas Insurance 1996 net falls.</title>
<headline>United Overseas Insurance 1996 net falls.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996 (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			     7.55  vs    8.25</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)		    12.50  vs   12.50</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		   18.50  vs   20.20</p>
<p>    Gross premium income		31.21  vs   30.00</p>
<p>    Gross investment income	    3.65  vs    3.55</p>
<p>    Profit from investment sales     3.19  vs    2.06</p>
<p>    Non-underwriting income	    6.92  vs    5.68</p>
<p>    Underwriting profit		  5.64  vs    6.93</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			10.27  vs   11.71</p>
<p>    Tax					2.72  vs    3.46</p>
<p>    Dividend pay date:   June 23, 1997</p>
<p>Last day books open: June 9, 1997</p>
<p>Note - United Overseas Insurance Ltd is a unit of the United Overseas Bank Group.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
</text>
